# tally 2.1.8 §4 (#169-h), E §5 step 1: a hole booking stays a hole movement until a version answers it, under cuts
# from that version's known, and the answer is its booking from then on, whatever reads it (E §3.2). pay[2026-02] is
# booked on 10 February with its amount a hole; v2, known 1 March, states 200.00 PLN: at cut 2026-06-30 the balance
# of 28 February (700.00), the field read (a1), a binding over its kind (n1, s1) all take 200.00 on its own day, and no
# adjustment is made (d1); at cut 2026-02-20 (b0) the hole stands. 2.1.7's refcore kept the hole at every cut.
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input amt[m in months]: money PLN question "Ile?"
input dom: int
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to world amount amt[m]

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  dom = 10 "s"
  amt[2026-01] = 100.00 PLN "s"
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-03-01
  amt[2026-02] = 200.00 PLN "s"

ask b1: bal(konto, 2026-02-28)
ask b0: bal(konto, 2026-02-28) as known 2026-02-20
ask a1: pay[2026-02].cash.amount
ask n1: count(p in transfers over 2026-02)
ask s1: sum(p.cash.amount for p in transfers over 2026-02)
ask d1: count(a in adjustments over 2026)
=== expect
a1: 200.00 PLN
  cut 2026-06-30
b0: ?"Ile?" (amt[2026-02])
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-01]
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-02]
  cut 2026-02-20
b1: 700.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-01]
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-02]
  cut 2026-06-30
d1: 0
  cut 2026-06-30
n1: 1
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-02]
  cut 2026-06-30
s1: 200.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-02]
  cut 2026-06-30
